hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18950","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, he said: I heard my father narrating from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he prayed at al-Batha, with a short spear before him, the Zuhr two rakahs and the Asr two rakahs, while a woman and a donkey would pass beyond it."
"18951","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out at midday to al-Batha and prayed the Zuhr two rakahs and the Asr two rakahs, with a short spear before him, and he performed ablution and the people began taking from the leftover of his ablution, and in the hadith of Awn: a woman and a donkey would pass beyond it."
"18952","Yazid narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Khalid, informed us, Abu Juhayfah narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the one among people most resembling him was al-Hasan ibn Ali."
"18953","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal and Umar ibn Abi Zaidah informed me, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer at al-Abtah, the Zuhr and the Asr, two rakahs two rakahs, with a short spear before him which he had set up before him, while people, a donkey, and a woman would pass beyond it."
"18954","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger at al-Abtah the Asr two rakahs."
"18955","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the one among people most resembling him was al-Hasan ibn Ali."
"18956","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to me, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray the Zuhr at al-Batha two rakahs and the Asr two rakahs, with a short spear before him, while a donkey and a woman would pass beyond it."
"18957","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Abtah the Asr two rakahs. He said: It was said to him: Like whom were you then He said: I used to pare arrows and feather them."
"18958","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Awn, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out in a red hullah, planted a short spear, and began praying toward it at al-Batha, while a dog, a donkey, and a woman would pass beyond it."
"18959","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah Wahb ibn Abdullah al-Suwai, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray at al-Abtah the Asr two rakahs, then he placed before him a short spear between him and the passersby, and I saw white hair on his anfaqah below his lower lip."
"18960","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray at al-Abtah the Asr prayer two rakahs."
"18961","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, he said: Abu Juhayfah informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not eat reclining."
"18962","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb al-Suwai, that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Abtah the Asr two rakahs."
"18963","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah informed me, he said: I saw my father buy a cupper and order the cupping vessels broken. He said: So I asked him about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a prostitute, and cursed the tattooer and the one tattooed, the eater of riba and its payer, and cursed the image-maker."
"18964","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed me, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out at midday. He said: So he performed ablution and the people began wiping themselves with the leftover of his ablution, then he prayed the Zuhr two rakahs, with a short spear before him."
"18965","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb, who is Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us at Mina, planted a short spear of his before him, and prayed with us two rakahs."
"18966","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: I saw Bilal calling the adhan and turning, and I kept following his mouth here and here, with his fingers in his ears. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in a red tent of his, I think of leather. He said: So Bilal went out before him with the short spear and planted it, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed. Abd al-Razzaq said: And I heard it at Makkah, he said: at al-Batha, while a dog, a woman, and a donkey would pass before him, wearing a red hullah, as if I am looking at the shine of his shins. Sufyan said: We think it was hibarah."
"18967","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I saw a red tent of leather belonging to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I saw Bilal go out with ablution water to pour it, so the people rushed to him; whoever took any of it wiped himself with it, and whoever found none of it took from the wetness of his companion hand. And I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, go out in a red hullah tucking it up, and I saw Bilal bring out a short spear, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed toward it, while beasts and people would pass beyond it."
"18968","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed toward a short spear or the like, with the road beyond it."
"18969","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Abtah while he was in a red tent of his. He said: So Bilal went out with the leftover of his ablution, some sprinkling and some receiving. He said: So Bilal called the adhan, and I kept following his mouth thus and thus, meaning right and left. He said: Then a short spear was planted for him. He said: So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out wearing a red jubbah of his, or a red hullah, and it is as if I am looking at the shine of his shins, and he led us toward the short spear in the Zuhr or the Asr two rakahs, while a woman, a dog, and a donkey would pass, not prevented. Then he kept praying two rakahs until he came to Madinah. And Waki once said: So he prayed the Zuhr two rakahs and the Asr two rakahs."
"18970","Waki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us from the dowry of a prostitute."
"18971","Waki narrated to us, from Misar and Sufyan, he said: my father, and Ibn Abi Zaidah, from his father, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not eat reclining."
"18972","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying at Mina two rakahs."
"18973","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I do not eat reclining."
"18974","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Hajjaj informed me, Shubah, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out at midday to al-Batha, performed ablution, and prayed the Zuhr two rakahs and the Asr two rakahs, with a short spear before him, and Awn added therein from his father Abu Juhayfah: and a donkey and a woman would pass beyond it. Hajjaj said in the hadith: Then the people stood and began taking his hand and wiping their faces with it. He said: So I took his hand and placed it on my face, and it was colder than snow and sweeter in scent than musk."
"18975","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, that he bought a cupper boy and ordered his cupping vessels broken. So I said to him: Are you breaking them He said: Yes, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the earnings of a prostitute, and cursed the eater of riba and its payer, the tattooer and the one tattooed, and cursed the image-maker."
"18976","Sulayman ibn Dawud and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and this of him, and he pointed to his anfaqah, white. So it was said to Abu Juhayfah: Like whom were you then He said: I used to pare arrows and feather them."
"18977","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Wahb al-Suwai, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was sent, and the Hour, like this from this, and it almost preceded it, and al-Amash joined the forefinger and the middle finger, and Muhammad once said: It almost preceded me."
"18978","And Abu al-Jawwab narrated it to us, Ammar narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Khalid, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I was sent from the Hour like this from this."
"18979","And Isa ibn Yunus said, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai, my father said: Ali ibn Bahr narrated it to us from him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointing with his finger."
